  "brief": "CrowdStrike to buy Zscaler in $44 billion all-stock deal, creating a cybersecurity giant.\n\nCrowdStrike / Zscaler (Announced): CrowdStrike to buy Zscaler. CrowdStrike is buying Zscaler for $44 billion [1, 2, 3]. The deal is expected to create a cybersecurity giant [8]. The acquisition is expected to be completed through an all-stock deal [5, 7].\nAmazon / Decart AI (Announced): Amazon to Acquire Decart AI. Amazon has agreed to acquire Decart AI for an estimated $7.5 billion [14, 15, 16]. The deal was announced by Amazon on November 23, 2023 [15, 18]. The acquisition is reportedly aimed at strengthening Amazon's trainium chip technology [16, 17].\nTexas Pacific Land / EagleRock Land (Announced): Texas Pacific Land and EagleRock Land Merger. Texas Pacific Land and EagleRock Land are merging in an all-equity deal [25, 24, 23]. The deal is worth $3 billion [23, 24, 22]. The companies have announced the merger [25, 24, 22].\nVerlinvest / Oatly (Announced): Verlinvest Offers for Oatly. Verlinvest is making a below-market offer for Oatly to satisfy Swedish takeover rules [27]. The offer is colliding with Swedish takeover rules, causing Oatly's stock to double [26]. The deal has been announced [26, 27].\nWorkday / C1.ai (Completed): Workday Completes C1.ai Acquisition. Workday has completed its acquisition of C1.ai [28, 29, 30]. The deal governs employee and AI agent access [28, 29, 30].\nABB / Ziehl-Abegg (Announced): ABB to Acquire German Fan Maker Ziehl-Abegg. ABB is acquiring German fan maker Ziehl-Abegg [31, 32, 33]. The deal is expected to double ABB's data center cooling business [31]. The acquisition is part of ABB's expansion into HVAC and industrial cooling applications [33].\nLinamar Corporation / Genie (Announced): Linamar to Acquire Genie from Terex. Linamar Corporation is acquiring Genie from Terex Corporation [34]. The deal will significantly expand Linamar's access to work platforms [34]. The acquisition was announced [34].\nTeledyne / Varex Imaging (Pending approval): Teledyne to Acquire Varex Imaging. Teledyne is acquiring Varex Imaging in an all-cash deal [36, 35]. The deal is pending regulatory approval [35]. Shareholders have already approved the merger agreement [36].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- Quantum Space completes its SPAC merger with $300 million and moves to the NYSE [37].\n- Townsquare Media board rejects $2.03-per-share takeover bid [38].\n- Varex Announces Financial Results for Fourth Quarter and Fiscal Year 2026 [39].",
